From d50e9aa1049f7520503c54d92016acd316167c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cheeseburger: Wi-Fi station: association and WPA2-PSK in the
 kernel (W6)

Port of topaz 0126/0129/0130 (TopazModem.cpp, APSL 2.0) to the cheeseburger WMI/HTT code:
the BSS table keeps beacon IEs; VDEV_START, PEER_CREATE, open-system AUTH, ASSOC REQ,
PEER_ASSOC + VDEV_UP, the WPA2-PSK 4-way handshake over the HTT data path (self-contained
SHA-1/HMAC/PBKDF2/PRF/AES key unwrap, checked against RFC 3394 and 802.11 annex vectors),
pairwise + group keys by VDEV_INSTALL_KEY, then one DHCP DISCOVER to prove the data path.
HTT TX for data (native wifi via the frag bank) and management (pkt type 3, tid 17) when
the WLAN.HL.1.0 firmware lacks WMI management TX (service 76), with TX completions.
Credentials from /var/local/wlan.conf on the phone (ssid=/psk=), never logged.
kern.sweetwlan_join (1 = after the first scan, 2 = rejoin now), kern.sweetwlan_mgmt.
