+/*
+ * Wi-Fi station for cheeseburger (OnePlus 5, WCN3990), W6 (0170): open-system auth, association,
+ * WPA2-PSK 4-way handshake in the kernel, keys by VDEV_INSTALL_KEY, then one DHCP DISCOVER to prove
+ * the data path both ways (the OFFER is logged).
+ *
+ * Port of topaz 0129/0130 (TopazModem.cpp, APSL 2.0; after topaz-woa assoc.c and Linux ath10k):
+ * VDEV_START on the AP's channel, PEER_CREATE, AUTH and ASSOC REQ as management frames, PEER_ASSOC +
+ * VDEV_UP, EAPOL over the HTT data path. Our WLAN.HL.1.0 firmware may lack WMI management TX
+ * (service 76): then management frames go over HTT as ath10k does (kern.sweetwlan_mgmt).
+ *
+ * Credentials: /var/local/wlan.conf on the phone ("ssid=NAME" and "psk=PASSPHRASE" lines), read after
+ * the first scan when kern.sweetwlan_join is 1; writing 2 asks for a (re)join. Never logged.
+ */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
